sible they could promote on  stations like good morning america which  walt disney owns and marvel studios has  been known to do this a lot they usually  show some clips from a movie on good  morning america at some point spider-man  knowing home is probably going to be one  of the biggest movies of all time if not  the biggest of all time so it would make  sense that they would promote it on gma  now there's no guarantee that this will  be on the 29th but it does seem like  sony and marvel studios definitely have  something in store for us on november  29th when tickets go on sale after all  all of these new tv spots are showing us  new footage but again the question now  is will they show toby and andrew in  this clip or in this final trailer and  my gut tells me i don't think so if sony  and marvel studios couldn't agree to  show the three spider-man in the main  trailer i'm pretty sure kevin feige  would get his way again for a final  trailer could they hint at him sure they  already have we've seen peter parker  saying that he's gonna need some help  and alfred molina basically already  confirmed toby maguire spider-man when  he says you're not peter to tom  holland's peter parker and that's of  course because he knows that his main  spider-man is tobey maguire then in  another tv spot we have tom holland's  peter parker saying the multiverse is  real so they're already doing some light  teasing or heavy teasing depending on  how you look at it but i don't think  they're gonna go full out and simply  show them i think they might hint at  them and i would really really love that  maybe two shadows maybe some theme songs  but not the big reveal and i'm okay with  that because i want to see that on  screen in the theaters for the first  time yeah we've known about toby and  andrew for a pretty long time now and  yes we've seen leaked photos but we  haven't seen them when they appear we  haven't seen them meet we have no real  interaction between them that's been  